  aboutHeading: "About Direction North",
  aboutParagraphs: [
    "Direction North is a Kochi-based manufacturer of retail display units, in-shop and outdoor branding, exhibition materials, and corporate gifts, delivering and installing across Kerala. Its range includes floor-standing display units, shelf wobblers, endcap branding, standees, backdrops, and custom awards, produced through an in-house design and manufacturing facility. The company serves sectors such as FMCG, pharma, telecom, quick-service restaurants, supermarkets, and automotive, and works from its office on Kadavanthra Road between 9:30 AM and 6:00 PM.",
    "The business has a particular marketing problem. Its best work is delivered inside other companies' stores. A finished installation makes a strong impression on the day, but afterwards it sits in a retail outlet where a new buyer will never see it. For a manufacturer selling to businesses, that finished work is the most convincing sales material it has, and it needed a place to be seen.",
    "This case study covers the Instagram and Facebook work delivered by Teknoppy: how finished projects are shown, how the profiles are run, and how enquiries are handled. It does not cover Direction North's manufacturing, installation, or pricing, which belong to the company."
  ],

  challengeLead: "Key challenges addressed during the social media engagement:",
  challenges: [
    {
      number: 1,
      title: "Finished work was hard to show",
      description: "Installations are completed offline, inside client stores. Without a plan to document and publish them, each project ended with the delivery instead of continuing as a sales asset."
    },
    {
      number: 2,
      title: "B2B buyers judge by proof, not slogans",
      description: "A brand manager choosing a display supplier wants to see real stores, real fixtures, and real results. General promotional posts do little for that buyer."
    },
    {
      number: 3,
      title: "A strong client list was not visible",
      description: "Having delivered for recognised retail brands is a powerful trust signal, but only if prospects can see it on the profiles they check."
    },
    {
      number: 4,
      title: "Profiles went quiet between projects",
      description: "A manufacturer's output is lumpy. Without an editorial calendar, the pages go silent, and a silent page makes a company look less active than it is."
    },
    {
      number: 5,
      title: "Enquiries arrive through messages and comments",
      description: "Buyers often ask a first question in a direct message. A slow or missing reply loses a lead that a phone call would have won."
    }
  ],

  objectiveLead: "Teknoppy was engaged to run Direction North's Instagram and Facebook so that completed projects work as a continuing portfolio and bring in qualified business enquiries. The brief centred on:",
